:name: custom_watch tier-1 sim
:description: Boots the custom_watch firmware ELF on an emulated nRF52840 DK — no hardware needed. Normally started via bin/watch-sim.sh, which builds the ELF, decodes the defmt stream, and feeds the canned NMEA fixture into the GPS UART. The ELF is the exact thumbv7em build that watch-flash.sh flashes; nothing is compiled differently for the simulator.

using sysbus

$elf ?= @apps/custom_watch/target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/release/app
$defmt_out ?= @/tmp/watch-sim/defmt.raw
$gps_pty ?= @/tmp/watch-sim/gps-pty

path add $ORIGIN

mach create "watch"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nrf52840dk_nrf52840.repl

# Sharp Memory LCD on SPIM2, chip-select on P1.12 (matches the pin map in
# boards/nrf52840_dk). The model is runtime-compiled C#; `showAnalyzer
# sysbus.spi2.display` (watch-sim.sh --gui) opens the live panel window.
include @SharpMipDisplay.cs
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString
"""
// SPIM3: the stock platform declares spi0..2 without EasyDMA and repl
// overlays can't change a constructor argument, but the 0x4002F000 slot
// (the dedicated high-speed SPIM the firmware uses for the display) is
// free to declare fresh with EasyDMA on. IRQ 47 per the datasheet.
spi3: SPI.NRF52840_SPI @ sysbus 0x4002F000
    easyDMA: true
    -> nvic@47

display: Video.SharpMipDisplay @ spi3

gpio1:
    12 -> display@0
"""

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
"""
runMacro $reset

include @defmt_rtt.py
setup_defmt_rtt $defmt_out

# LED1 (P0.13) blinks at 1 Hz from ui::blink_task — echo each state change
# into the Renode log as a scheduler-liveness signal.
python
"""
led = monitor.Machine["sysbus.gpio0.led0"]

def led_changed(led, state):
    led.InfoLog("LED1 %s" % ("on" if state else "off"))

led.StateChanged += led_changed
"""

# GPS rail: the u-blox breakout's NMEA stream arrives on uart0 (UARTE0).
# The pty end is where the host feeder writes canned sentences. The firmware
# consumes them once step 3 of README.md (GNSS bring-up) lands; until then
# the emulated UARTE discards them. Kept as the LAST setup command: monitor
# errors don't reach the Renode log file, so bin/watch-sim.sh treats the pty
# symlink appearing as proof the whole script executed.
emulation CreateUartPtyTerminal "gps" $gps_pty true
connector Connect sysbus.uart0 gps

start
